    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
      Singapore has long been heralded as a premier global hub for business, and a significant part of that reputation is built upon its incredibly competitive, transparent, and straightforward tax regime. At the heart of this framework is the headline corporate tax rate of <strong>17%</strong>. Coupled with a single-tier territorial framework, generous startup exemptions, and an extensive international network of tax treaties, Singapore continues to be the preferred headquarters location for multinational corporations and ambitious high-growth startups alike.
    </p>

    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
      As corporate tax advisors who have guided hundreds of founders through their expansion into Southeast Asia, we understand that corporate taxation is rarely just a numbers game. It's about predictability, cash flow management, and ultimately, peace of mind. Founders and finance teams often approach us feeling overwhelmed by compliance deadlines—from ECI to Form C-S. In this comprehensive 2026 guide, we break down every facet of Singapore’s corporate tax system with deep empathy for the operational realities of running a business, giving you actionable strategies to optimize your tax position legally and efficiently.
    </p>

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6 dark:border-overlay-light dark:bg-surface">
